Distribution terms for programs you create

The copyright in executable files (EXE files, DLL files) produced by the
ActBa64 compiler, and in any development files the user creates, belongs to
the user who created the program.

Programs created by the user (source code, executable files and other program
resources) may be distributed by the user. There are no restrictions on
commercial use. You do not need to contact bellyoshi when distributing them.

As an additional permission, the portions of ActBa64's libraries (such as the
files under Include) that are compiled into or linked into an executable file
produced by the ActBa64 compiler may be distributed as part of that executable
file without including the above copyright notice and permission notice.

